    "title": "How cheese can kill you - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Knapton ,\n14 hours ago At the turn of the century, milk-borne epidemics were rife, with up to a third of London milk contaminated with the pus of diseased cows, manure and dirt. Hundreds of thousands of people died from deadly bacteria in milk and cheese, but with the widespread roll-out of pasteurisation in the 1930s and 40s, fatalities plummeted, and the problem seemed solved. Read full article",
